Z||000071||2birds||02-25-2001||04:53 PM||||I always understood scrapple (RAPA brand, at least) to be pork by-products (like I said, everything but the squeal), corn meal, and sage.  Probably some lard to hold it all together.  You just use corn meal to extend regular sausage.  Comes in a one or two pound brick.<BR>I grew up eating scrapple for breakfast (in Maryland), but when I moved to Iowa, we couldn't find it anywhere.  My wife (a native Iowan) won't touch it.  Of course, she used to eat peanut butter and mayonnaise sandwiches when we first got married.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
